{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, serve a usable package repository whose repository content is stored locally.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A local package and APT metadata were created under /srv/local-apt with matching SHA-256 values. The enabled service served that content over port 8080, returned HTTP 200, and remained available after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-950b2c785ceb4299","cmd-7dfd46a69c54467f","cmd-486f5490a61949e0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while the usual remote repositories are unreachable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Fresh isolated indexes showed the Ubuntu archive and security endpoints failing through an unreachable proxy while the local repository succeeded. APT then fetched local-repo-demo 1.0 from node1, installed it, and ran its executable successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-681e191b17bf4dec","cmd-c7a9cabbfbd445e5","cmd-c79355baaf3d4fcf"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system remained Ubuntu 24.04.3 with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic before and after execution. The repository used already-available platform tools, and the installed all-architecture package executed successfully.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-d748c0b44dfa483c","cmd-c7a9cabbfbd445e5","cmd-486f5490a61949e0","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.78,"summary":"No causally unrelated state-changing experiment was identified: repository construction, service/source configuration, isolation, installation, restart, and recovery checks all supported the task or mandatory evidence protocol. Hygiene is reduced because the isolation command left a persistent dead proxy that continues blocking ordinary HTTP APT repositories after the demonstration, rather than limiting or restoring the outage simulation (cmd-681e191b17bf4dec; persistence confirmed by cmd-c79355baaf3d4fcf). Final evidence collection also left /tmp/post-reboot-proof.deb and /tmp/post-reboot-apt-lists behind; these bounded, low-risk artifacts were not cleaned up (cmd-486f5490a61949e0, cmd-c79355baaf3d4fcf, global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files). The service also produced systemd's warning that using the special nobody account is unsafe, although no service failure resulted (cmd-7dfd46a69c54467f). Package health remained sound and there were no failed services.","evidence_ids":["cmd-681e191b17bf4dec","cmd-7dfd46a69c54467f","cmd-486f5490a61949e0","cmd-c79355baaf3d4fcf","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The provider-wide restart protocol is also strong: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, an acknowledged scheduled reboot followed by connection loss, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered system, repository, artifact, package, and APT provenance. Fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot-ID change and unchanged platform.","limitations":["The repository is trusted without a signature and served over plain HTTP, but repository signing or transport security was not part of the public contract.","The retained APT proxy configuration means the evidence does not show ordinary remote repository access being restored after the bounded installation test."]}
